# Extra (non-stock) map downloads.
#
# The server already ships with the classic retail CS 1.6 map pool
# (de_dust2, de_dust, de_train, de_aztec, de_cbble, de_inferno, de_nuke,
# de_prodigy, de_survivor, de_vertigo, cs_assault, cs_italy, cs_office) —
# see server/config/mapcycle.txt. Those need nothing extra.
#
# Popular community maps like fy_iceworld, ka_rats/kaos_rats, awp_india,
# 35hp_2, etc. are NOT part of the official install — they're fan-made
# files spread across many sites with unclear/mixed redistribution rights,
# so we don't hardcode download links here. Instead:
#
#   1. Find the map yourself from a source you trust (e.g. GameBanana's
#      Counter-Strike 1.6 map section, a community forum, or a friend's
#      server's own map pack).
#   2. Copy this file to maps-list.txt (same folder) and add one line
#      per map:
#
#        mapname=https://example.com/path/to/mapname.zip
#
#      - The URL may point to a .zip (containing the .bsp and any
#        matching .res/.txt/.wad resource files) or directly to a .bsp.
#      - `mapname` must match the .bsp filename without extension, and
#        is what you'll type in mapcycle.txt / the panel's map switcher.
#
#   3. Restart the cs-server container (or run
#      docker compose exec cs-server /server/scripts/download-maps.sh).
#      Already-downloaded maps are skipped, so this is safe to re-run.
#
# You can also skip this entirely and just drop .bsp (+ .res/.txt/.wad)
# files straight into the ./maps/ folder on the host — they get synced
# into the server's maps directory on every container start either way.
#
# Example (uncomment and point at a source you trust):
# fy_iceworld=https://example.com/maps/fy_iceworld.zip
# ka_rats=https://example.com/maps/ka_rats.zip
